#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""A supervised first run of `homezc`, the index-pulse ("zero-cross") homing program, on the real controller.

    scripts/a465-homezc --check                          # no motion: is the program there, and does the controller load it?
    scripts/a465-homezc 6                                # index-home joint 6 (speed 5, time limit 8 s)
    scripts/a465-homezc 6 --speed 5 --time-limit 8

Stand at the E-stop for a run on an axis. Joints 1 to 6 only; 7 and 8 are refused before the port is opened.

What it does, in order: stops scripts/a465-padjog if it is running; opens the port exclusively and checks for
the `$` prompt; logs everything in both directions to sessions/<time>-homezc.log; makes sure /tmp/homezc on the
controller equals sessions/controller-files/patched/homezc by `cksum` (size and byte sum), uploading it with
a465/aci.py if not. Then:

  --check   runs the program with no argument. It must print "invalid command line arguments." and a usage
            line and exit; that shows the controller loads and runs it. No axis is ever sent.
  <axis>    reads the joint angles (`w2`) and the status words (`axst`), sets `speed`, announces the move and
            runs `/tmp/homezc <axis>` in the foreground. If the program asks for the PAUSE/CONTINUE button it
            says so in capitals and waits up to 180 s; the time limit starts once that is over (or from the
            command, if the request never appears). If the prompt is not back within the limit it sends Ctrl-Z
            once, says HALTED, waits out the reset and, if there is still no prompt, sends Ctrl-E. Ctrl-C from
            you sends Ctrl-Z. However it ends, it reads the angles and status words again and prints a summary:
            degrees moved, status bits 5, 6, 11 and 8/9/10 before and after, the program's own output, how
            long it ran, whether it was halted.

Exit code 0 only if the program returned by itself without printing anything but the button request
(the plain `homezc` prints only "Homing axis N...Ok."; the offset-printing copy adds "zero-cross offset: K").
Measured 2026-11-24: it moves in the + counts direction to the next index pulse, less than one motor turn.
"""
import os
import sys

REPO = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))
sys.path.insert(0, REPO)

from a465 import homezc      # noqa: E402

if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(homezc.main(repo=REPO))
